    {
      "id": "claim_cb2f9cbb7e8d4fad9b4fb656114a6ee6",
      "statement": "'案 I' (2026-09-02) found that a marker tag literal can itself be split across a terminal line-wrap boundary, causing a strict contiguous-byte match to miss the CLOSE tag, latch the parser into 'inside a block' indefinitely, and silently drop up to roughly 31% of a session's terminal output until a 32KB safety-valve forced a reset; the fix (matchMarkerAllowingWrap) matches marker characters while skipping CR/LF/space/tab/complete ANSI escape sequences between them but treats any interposed printable character as a non-match.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://web/src/app/hub-marker-filter.ts#L63-L84",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:d88761cd3642cee2f7f97c9cb45d96fe39fd67c1cbf038d749047e1a82b84e1b:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_306a001abac442abab67261988e8206e",
      "statement": "'案 J' (2026-09-03) removed the last 'discard output until CLOSE is seen' state machine after finding that on an alternate screen a redraw can contain an OPEN tag whose matching CLOSE is never drawn at all in that frame (not wrapped, genuinely absent), which no wrap-tolerant matching could find; after this change there is no code path that buffers and discards terminal output, so display can never freeze waiting for a CLOSE that never arrives.",
